<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fauj-i-Ain</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Fauj-i-Ain was the regular standing army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a>, created by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Ranjit Singh</a>. Trained along European lines, partly by European officers, it combined disciplined infantry, artillery and cavalry and was the main engine of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> expansion. It later became a powerful political force after Ranjit Singh's death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fauj-i-ain.jpg" alt="Fauj-i-Ain" width="320" height="141" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles Singh · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sikh_Regular_Infantry_standard.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
